Objectives:

1.To understand the concept and structure of an AVL tree.
2.To implement insertion operations in an AVL tree using C++.
3.To calculate the balance factor of each node.
4.To identify the LL imbalance caused by inserting elements in the left subtree.
5.To perform right rotation to balance the tree.
6.To display the elements of the balanced AVL tree using inorder traversal.
7.To understand how AVL trees maintain balance and improve searching efficiency.


Changed Objectives:

1.To understand the concept and working of an AVL tree.
2.To insert elements into an AVL tree using Binary Search Tree insertion rules.
3.To detect an LL imbalance after inserting elements.
4.To perform right rotation to balance the AVL tree.
5.To display the tree structure before and after rotation.
6.To calculate and display the balance factors of affected nodes.
7.To accept a user-defined sequence and identify whether it causes an LL imbalance.
8.To test the program using different input sequences and edge cases.
